 # Spatial Hashing
 
-Also called: Hierarchical Spatial Hash, Octal Spatial Hash
 
 ## Overview
-Spatial Hashing maps 3D world positions to hierarchical string-based spatial hashes (keys) and vice versa, enabling efficient traversal of a voxel hierarchy without storing explicit grid structures [S1, unofficial]. It differs from flat spatial hashing by using a fixed-depth 12-level octal encoding where each character represents a 2x2x2 voxel block, allowing direct conversion between coordinates and region boundaries [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Bitstream Voxel Position Encoding](2371-bitstream-voxel-position-encoding.md) which stores raw bits, this method compresses position into a human-readable string for hierarchical queries [S1, unofficial].
+Spatial Hashing maps 3D world positions to hierarchical string-based spatial hashes and vice versa, enabling efficient traversal of a voxel hierarchy without storing explicit grid structures [S1, unofficial]. It differs from flat spatial hashing by using a fixed-depth 12-level octal encoding where each character represents a 2×2×2 voxel block, allowing direct conversion between coordinates and region boundaries [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** A 3D position (Vector3 with X, Y, Z coordinates) or a spatial hash string (1-12 octal digits).
-**Outputs:** A spatial hash string (for position input) or 3D coordinates/region bounds (for hash input).
+**Inputs:** A 3D position (Vector3 with X, Y, Z coordinates) or a spatial hash string (1–12 octal digits) [S1, unofficial].
+**Outputs:** A spatial hash string (for position input) or 3D coordinates/region bounds (for hash input) [S1, unofficial].
 
